NOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.' AND choices_json IS '["Create a relationship between the Date table and the Sales table.","Disable the auto date/time option.","Create a Date table and select Mark as Date Table.","Disable the load on the Date table.","Remove the relationship between the Product table and the Sales table."]' AND correct_json IS '[0,2]' AND explanation IS 'The intended source selections are A and C: create/mark an explicit Date table and relate it to Sales. Do not infer that marking one date table removes every hidden auto date/time table for other eligible columns. Order Date becomes the many side of a relationship, while unconnected Ship Date and Delivered Date can remain eligible when Auto date/time stays on. For guaranteed removal of all automatic tables, disable Auto date/time after building and wiring a replacement and migrating dependent visuals. The choose-two source is not a complete migration checklist.' AND image IS '/exhibit-assets/f1-109-108.webp' AND answer_image IS NULL AND context IS NULL AND rows_json IS NULL) OR (prompt IS 'You have a Power BI data model that analyzes product sales over time. The data model contains the following

tables.

A one-to-many relationship exists between the tables.

